# Line endings are LF in the repository and LF in every working tree, on every
# platform. The build depends on it: the Electron shell revision that decides
# whether a release can install as a silent core-only update is a hash of the
# shell sources, computed on the Linux runner and re-asserted on the macOS and
# Windows packaging runners. A checkout that materialised CRLF there would fail
# that assertion and take the whole release build down with it.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binaries are never touched. Git detects these on its own; naming them removes
# the guess for the assets that feed the shell revision.
*.png binary
*.ico binary
*.icns binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
*.ttf binary
*.exe binary
